# API Conventions

## URL Pattern

```
/api/v1/{resource}
/api/v1/{resource}/{id}
/api/v1/{resource}/{id}/{sub-resource}
```

## Minimal API Endpoint Pattern

```csharp
public static class StudentEndpoints
{
    public static void Map(IEndpointRouteBuilder app)
    {
        var group = app.MapGroup("/api/v1/students")
            .WithTags("Students")
            .RequireAuthorization();

        group.MapPost("/", CreateStudentEndpoint.Handle);
        group.MapGet("/", ListStudentsEndpoint.Handle);
        group.MapGet("/{id:guid}", GetStudentEndpoint.Handle);
        group.MapPut("/{id:guid}", UpdateStudentEndpoint.Handle);
        group.MapDelete("/{id:guid}", DeleteStudentEndpoint.Handle);
    }
}
```

## Response Rules

- Success: return DTO directly or `Results.Ok(dto)`
- Business failure: `Results.BadRequest(problemDetails)` from `Result.Errors`
- Not found: `Results.NotFound()`
- Forbidden: `Results.Forbid()` — RBAC denial

## Endpoint Responsibilities

- Bind request → command/query → `IMediator.Send()` → map `Result` to HTTP
- **No business logic in endpoints**

## Pagination

- List endpoints: `?page=1&pageSize=20&search=&sortBy=`
- Return `{ items, totalCount, page, pageSize }`

## Swagger

- Every endpoint needs `.WithName()`, `.Produces<T>()`, `.ProducesProblem()`
